From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] waflib/Utils.py: mark a regex as a raw string

Python emits a SyntaxWarning for the invalid escape sequence '\d' in
this non-raw string. do_configure runs `waf --version` and parses its
stdout for a version number; the warning text, printed to the same
stream, gets picked up by the parser instead of the version, causing:

  ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'SyntaxWarning'

Upstream-Status: Backport
Signed-off-by: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
---
 waflib/Utils.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/waflib/Utils.py b/waflib/Utils.py
--- a/waflib/Utils.py
+++ b/waflib/Utils.py
@@ -411,5 +411,5 @@
 	if s=='cli'and os.name=='nt':
 		return'win32'
-	return re.split('\d+$',s)[0]
+	return re.split(r'\d+$',s)[0]
 def nada(*k,**kw):
 	pass
--
2.34.1
